(a) Examples of such substances (allergens), any two:
- **dust**;
- **pollen**;
- **animal dander**;
- **mites** (in dust);
- perfume or fungal spores.

(b) The body produces antibodies of the **IgE** type in response to these allergens.

(c) Role of mast cells: on exposure to the allergen, the IgE-coated **mast cells release chemicals such as histamine and serotonin**. These chemicals cause the symptoms of the allergic response, such as sneezing, watery eyes, running nose and difficulty in breathing (wheezing).
